## THE MEASURED LOSING RUN — 6 consecutive losers is the worst over 10 days
| the rule | leverage | 6 straight worst-case stops cost | survives? |
|---|---|---|---|
| live now: fixed 66,000 coins at 0.18291 on $888 | 13.595x | **54.19 %** of equity | yes |
| 2 % risk, LIVE stop 0.70 + 0.1975 drag = 0.8975 worst | 2.228x | **11.42 %** of equity | yes |
| 2 % risk, SCORED stop 0.80 + 0.1975 = 0.9975 worst | 2.005x | **11.42 %** of equity | yes |
| max L holding max DD <= 25 % | 4.800x | **25.50 %** of equity | yes |
| max L holding max DD <= 50 % | 10.700x | **49.20 %** of equity | yes |

- L at which ONE worst trade wipes the account: **111.4x** at the 0.70 stop, **100.3x** at 0.80
- the fixed-coin size is not a risk rule: 66,000 coins is a CONSTANT NOTIONAL, so the fraction
  of equity it risks changes every time equity or price moves. At $888 it is 13.595x; the same
  66,000 coins on the $500 the ledger started from was 24.1x.
